IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 (Western Australia) -- which days are public holidays (and bank holidays) in WA in
-- a given year: the days fixed by s 5 and the Second Schedule, the extra days when a holiday falls on a weekend,
-- Western Australia Day and Labour Day, the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed, the Governor's special and substituted
-- days (ss 7, 8), Saturdays as bank holidays (s 6), bank closing (s 10), and how a WA industrial instrument and a
-- proclamation stand against the Act (ss 3, 9).
--
-- SEAT: the employee in Western Australia. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it: "On what day does
-- this holiday fall", "What are the public holidays in WA this year", "Is this day a public holiday for me in WA",
-- "Is this day a bank holiday", "Does my award or this Act prevail".
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3(1)-(3), s 5, s 6, s 7(1), s 8(1), s 9, s 10, and the Second Schedule (every listed day and
-- the four weekend rules).
--
-- Edition: the compilation including amendments to the Industrial Relations Legislation Amendment Act 2021 Pt 6
-- (No. 30 of 2021, in force 12 February 2022), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_44571.txt
-- (retrieved 7 September 2026). No regulations. The day for the "Celebration Day for the Anniversary of the Birthday
-- of the Reigning Sovereign" is "appointed for each year by proclamation published in the Government Gazette": no
-- proclamation is deposited, so that date is an INPUT. Proclamations under ss 7 and 8 are likewise inputs.
--
-- Good Friday, Easter Sunday and Easter Monday are named but not defined by the Act. The encoding computes Easter
-- Sunday by the Gregorian (Western church) reckoning -- an ENCODER'S CHOICE, not in the deposit.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: public half-holidays under s 7(1)(b) (no time of day is modelled); the district or locality limits of
-- ss 7 and 8 beyond asking whether a proclamation reaches the place where I work; the 3-week Gazette notice periods of
-- ss 7(2), 8(2), (3) (whether a proclamation is valid is taken as given); whether an employee must work, or is paid,
-- on a public holiday -- that is the Fair Work Act 2009 ss 114-116 or the employee's industrial instrument, not this
-- Act. Machinery out: ss 1, 2; the omitted s 4 and First Schedule.
--
-- CONSISTENCY with the Fair Work Act 2009 baseline (fwa-employee.l4, s 115): there, Western Australia Day and Labour
-- Day are public holidays "if my State's law declares it a public holiday". This encoding is that State law: both are
-- declared by s 5 and the Second Schedule, every year. Easter Sunday and the weekend extra days are not named in
-- s 115(1)(a); they reach the employee through s 115(1)(b) ("declared or prescribed by or under a law of a State").
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 -- the employee's questions`

§§ `The days of the week`

-- daydate's `Weekday of` counts Sunday as 0, Monday 1, ... Saturday 6.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls on a Saturday or Sunday` IF
    `Weekday of` `the day` EQUALS 6 OR `Weekday of` `the day` EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Saturday` IF `Weekday of` `the day` EQUALS 6

-- "Monday on or first Monday following" the day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Monday on or first Monday following` MEANS
    `the day` PLUS ((8 MINUS `Weekday of` `the day`) MODULO 7)

-- "the next following Tuesday": strictly after the day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next following Tuesday after` MEANS
    `the day` PLUS (((8 MINUS `Weekday of` `the day`) MODULO 7) PLUS 1)

§§ `Easter -- an encoder's choice`

-- The Act names "Good Friday", "Easter Sunday" and "Easter Monday" and does not say how Easter is fixed. The encoding
-- uses the Gregorian computus (the anonymous Gregorian algorithm), which gives the Western churches' Easter Sunday.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Easter Sunday in` MEANS
    Date ((r MODULO 31) PLUS 1) (FLOOR (r DIVIDED BY 31)) `the year`
    WHERE
        a MEANS `the year` MODULO 19
        b MEANS FLOOR (`the year` DIVIDED BY 100)
        c MEANS `the year` MODULO 100
        d MEANS FLOOR (b DIVIDED BY 4)
        e MEANS b MODULO 4
        f MEANS FLOOR ((b PLUS 8) DIVIDED BY 25)
        g MEANS FLOOR ((b MINUS f PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 3)
        h MEANS ((19 TIMES a) PLUS b MINUS d MINUS g PLUS 15) MODULO 30
        i MEANS FLOOR (c DIVIDED BY 4)
        k MEANS c MODULO 4
        l MEANS (32 PLUS (2 TIMES e) PLUS (2 TIMES i) MINUS h MINUS k) MODULO 7
        m MEANS FLOOR ((a PLUS (11 TIMES h) PLUS (22 TIMES l)) DIVIDED BY 451)
        r MEANS h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES m) PLUS 114

§§ `s 5 and the Second Schedule -- the days`

-- s 5: "Subject to this Act, the several days specified, or appointed under the power, in the Second Schedule shall be
-- public holidays and bank holidays throughout the State."
-- Second Schedule: "New Year's Day (1st January). Australia Day (26th January or, when that day falls on a Saturday or
-- Sunday, the first Monday following the 26th January). Labour Day (Monday on or first Monday following the 1st March).
-- Good Friday. Easter Sunday. Easter Monday. Anzac Day (25th April). Western Australia Day (Monday on or first Monday
-- following the 1st June). Celebration Day for the Anniversary of the Birthday of the Reigning Sovereign (day to be
-- appointed for each year by proclamation ...). Christmas Day (25th December). Boxing Day (26th December)."
-- "When New Year's Day, Anzac Day, or Christmas Day falls on a Saturday or Sunday the next following Monday is also a
-- public holiday and bank holiday. When Boxing Day falls on a Saturday the next following Monday is also a public
-- holiday and bank holiday. When Boxing Day falls on a Sunday or Monday the next following Tuesday is also a public
-- holiday and bank holiday."
-- The extra days are listed straight after the day they follow, so a year's list comes out in date order (save for
-- the Sovereign's birthday, which falls where the proclamation puts it).
DECLARE Holiday IS ONE OF
    `New Year's Day`
    `the Monday after New Year's Day`              -- "also" a holiday when 1 January is a Saturday or Sunday
    `Australia Day`                                -- moved, not doubled: the 26th itself is then no holiday
    `Labour Day`
    `Good Friday`
    `Easter Sunday`
    `Easter Monday`
    `Anzac Day`
    `the Monday after Anzac Day`                   -- "also" a holiday when 25 April is a Saturday or Sunday
    `Western Australia Day`
    `the Sovereign's birthday`                     -- the "Celebration Day for the Anniversary of the Birthday of the Reigning Sovereign": the King's Birthday
    `Christmas Day`
    `Boxing Day`
    `the Monday after Christmas Day`               -- "also" a holiday when 25 December is a Saturday or Sunday
    `the Monday after Boxing Day`                  -- "also" a holiday when 26 December is a Saturday
    `the Tuesday after Boxing Day`                 -- "also" a holiday when 26 December is a Sunday or Monday

DECLARE `When it falls` IS ONE OF
    `falls on`
        HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `does not arise this year`                     -- an extra day whose weekend condition is not met that year

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `When it falls`
`only if` MEANS
    IF `the condition` THEN `falls on` `the day` ELSE `does not arise this year`

@export On what day does this public holiday fall in WA in a given year (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 s 5, Second Schedule)?
GIVEN `the holiday` IS A Holiday @desc Which holiday in the Second Schedule, or which weekend extra day
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year, for example 2024
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `When it falls`
DECIDE `On what day does this holiday fall` IS
    CONSIDER `the holiday`
    WHEN `New Year's Day` THEN `falls on` newYear
    WHEN `the Monday after New Year's Day`
        THEN `only if` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` newYear) (`falls on a Saturday or Sunday` newYear)
    WHEN `Australia Day` THEN
        IF `falls on a Saturday or Sunday` australia
            THEN `falls on` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` australia)
            ELSE `falls on` australia
    WHEN `Labour Day` THEN `falls on` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` (Date 1 3 `the year`))
    WHEN `Good Friday` THEN `falls on` (easter MINUS 2)
    WHEN `Easter Sunday` THEN `falls on` easter
    WHEN `Easter Monday` THEN `falls on` (easter PLUS 1)
    WHEN `Anzac Day` THEN `falls on` anzac
    WHEN `the Monday after Anzac Day`
        THEN `only if` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` anzac) (`falls on a Saturday or Sunday` anzac)
    WHEN `Western Australia Day` THEN `falls on` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` (Date 1 6 `the year`))
    WHEN `the Sovereign's birthday` THEN `falls on` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`
    WHEN `Christmas Day` THEN `falls on` christmas
    WHEN `Boxing Day` THEN `falls on` boxing
    WHEN `the Monday after Christmas Day`
        THEN `only if` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` christmas) (`falls on a Saturday or Sunday` christmas)
    WHEN `the Monday after Boxing Day`
        THEN `only if` (`the Monday on or first Monday following` boxing) (`is a Saturday` boxing)
    WHEN `the Tuesday after Boxing Day`
        THEN `only if` (`the next following Tuesday after` boxing)
                       (`Weekday of` boxing EQUALS 0 OR `Weekday of` boxing EQUALS 1)
    WHERE
        newYear   MEANS Date 1 1 `the year`
        australia MEANS Date 26 1 `the year`
        anzac     MEANS Date 25 4 `the year`
        christmas MEANS Date 25 12 `the year`
        boxing    MEANS Date 26 12 `the year`
        easter    MEANS `Easter Sunday in` `the year`

`every holiday in the Schedule` MEANS
    LIST `New Year's Day`, `the Monday after New Year's Day`, `Australia Day`, `Labour Day`, `Good Friday`,
         `Easter Sunday`, `Easter Monday`, `Anzac Day`, `the Monday after Anzac Day`, `Western Australia Day`,
         `the Sovereign's birthday`, `Christmas Day`, `Boxing Day`, `the Monday after Christmas Day`,
         `the Monday after Boxing Day`, `the Tuesday after Boxing Day`

GIVEN `the falling` IS A `When it falls`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the day, if any` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the falling`
    WHEN `falls on` d THEN LIST d
    WHEN `does not arise this year` THEN EMPTY

GIVEN `the falling` IS A `When it falls`, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `lands on` IF elem `the day` (`the day, if any` `the falling`)

-- Two Schedule days can land on one date (Easter Monday on Anzac Day, 2011; Christmas Day's extra Monday on Boxing
-- Day itself, whenever 25 December is a Sunday). The Schedule gives no further day for the clash: it is one day off.
@export What are the public holidays in WA in a given year (s 5, Second Schedule), as dates?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year, for example 2024
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
DECIDE `What are the public holidays in WA this year` IS
    nub (concat (map (GIVEN h YIELD `the day, if any` (`On what day does this holiday fall` h `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`))
                   `every holiday in the Schedule`))

@export How many days are public holidays in WA in a given year under the Schedule?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year, for example 2024
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many public holidays in WA this year` IS
    count (`What are the public holidays in WA this year` `the year` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)

@export Which Schedule holidays fall on this day in WA?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day, ISO 8601
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A LIST OF Holiday
DECIDE `Which holidays fall on this day` IS
    filter (GIVEN h YIELD `lands on` (`On what day does this holiday fall` h (DATE_YEAR `the day`) `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`) `the day`)
           `every holiday in the Schedule`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Schedule holiday` IF
    elem `the day` (`What are the public holidays in WA this year` (DATE_YEAR `the day`) `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`)

§§ `ss 7 and 8 -- the Governor's proclamations`

-- s 7(1): "The Governor may, from time to time, by proclamation -- (a) appoint a special day specified in the
-- proclamation to be a public holiday or bank holiday, or both ... in any year either throughout the State or within
-- such district or locality as is specified in the proclamation".
-- s 8(1): "The Governor may ... by proclamation declare that, instead of a day referred to in section 5, some other day
-- shall be a public holiday or bank holiday, or both ... and in that case such other day shall accordingly be a public
-- holiday ... instead of the day so referred to in that section."
-- Whether the Governor has proclaimed, and whether the proclamation reaches the place where I work, are facts the
-- employee states (from the Gazette); the encoding does not guess them.
DECLARE `Public holiday answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a public holiday under s 5 and the Second Schedule`
    `yes: a public holiday instead of a Schedule day, by proclamation under s 8`
    `yes: a special public holiday by proclamation under s 7`
    `no: the Governor has moved this day's holiday to another day under s 8`
    `no: not a public holiday in WA`

@export Is this day a public holiday for me in WA (Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 ss 5, 7, 8)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day, ISO 8601
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
      `if a s 7 proclamation makes this day a special public holiday where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Governor has by proclamation under s 7 appointed this day a special public holiday, throughout the State or in the district where you work
      `if a s 8 proclamation makes this day a public holiday instead of a Schedule day where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Governor has by proclamation under s 8 declared this day a public holiday in place of a Schedule day, for the place where you work
      `if a s 8 proclamation moves this day's holiday to another day where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Governor has by proclamation under s 8 moved the Schedule holiday on this day to some other day, for the place where you work
GIVETH A `Public holiday answer`
DECIDE `Is this day a public holiday for me in WA` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `if a s 8 proclamation makes this day a public holiday instead of a Schedule day where I work`
            THEN `yes: a public holiday instead of a Schedule day, by proclamation under s 8`
        IF `is a Schedule holiday` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`
           AND `if a s 8 proclamation moves this day's holiday to another day where I work`
            THEN `no: the Governor has moved this day's holiday to another day under s 8`
        IF `is a Schedule holiday` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`
            THEN `yes: a public holiday under s 5 and the Second Schedule`
        IF `if a s 7 proclamation makes this day a special public holiday where I work`
            THEN `yes: a special public holiday by proclamation under s 7`
        OTHERWISE `no: not a public holiday in WA`

§§ `ss 5, 6 and 10 -- bank holidays`

-- s 5: the Schedule days are "public holidays and bank holidays". s 6: "Saturday shall be a bank holiday throughout
-- the State." s 10(1): "all banks in the State shall close their premises to the public on bank holidays"; (2) not
-- on a Saturday that "(a) is a bank holiday by virtue of section 6; and (b) is not a bank holiday or public holiday
-- under any other section." Proclamations under ss 7, 8 are left out of these two questions.
@export Is this day a bank holiday in WA (ss 5, 6)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day, ISO 8601
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day a bank holiday in WA` IF
    `is a Schedule holiday` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` OR `is a Saturday` `the day`

@export Must the bank where I work close its premises to the public on this day (s 10)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day, ISO 8601
      `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc The day appointed for that year by proclamation in the Government Gazette for the King's Birthday, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my bank close to the public on this day` IF
    `is a Schedule holiday` `the day` `the Sovereign's birthday as proclaimed`

§§ `ss 3 and 9 -- my industrial instrument against the Act`

-- s 3(1): "Unless it is otherwise expressly provided in this Act, any provision of an award, order, or industrial
-- agreement made under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 or an employer-employee agreement ... (an industrial
-- instrument) prevails over a provision of or under this Act to the extent of any inconsistency".
-- s 3(3): "a provision of an industrial instrument is of no effect to the extent that it substitutes another day for
-- the Easter Sunday public holiday solely because Easter Sunday falls on a weekend."
-- s 9: "Any provision of a proclamation made under section 7 or 8 prevails over any provision of an award, order, or
-- industrial agreement made under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 to the extent of any inconsistency therewith."
-- An instrument under the Fair Work Act 2009 (a modern award, an enterprise agreement) is not "made under the
-- Industrial Relations Act 1979"; s 3 does not speak to it. Whether provisions are inconsistent is a fact asked.
DECLARE `Which prevails` IS ONE OF
    `not decided by this Act: s 3 reaches only instruments under the WA Industrial Relations Act 1979`
    `this Act: a substitute day for Easter Sunday because it falls on a weekend has no effect (s 3(3))`
    `no inconsistency: both apply`
    `the proclamation (s 9)`
    `my industrial instrument (s 3(1))`

@export Does my industrial instrument or the Public and Bank Holidays Act prevail on public holidays (ss 3, 9)?
GIVEN `if my instrument is made under the WA Industrial Relations Act 1979` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your award, order, industrial agreement or employer-employee agreement was made under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 (WA), not the Fair Work Act 2009
      `if it is inconsistent with the provision of or under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your instrument says something different from the Act (or a proclamation under it) about the day
      `if that provision is in a proclamation under s 7 or 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Act-side provision is a proclamation of the Governor under s 7 or s 8
      `if it substitutes another day for Easter Sunday solely because Easter Sunday falls on a weekend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the inconsistency is that your instrument moves the Easter Sunday holiday to another day only because it is on a weekend
GIVETH A `Which prevails`
DECIDE `Does my award or this Act prevail` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `if my instrument is made under the WA Industrial Relations Act 1979`
            THEN `not decided by this Act: s 3 reaches only instruments under the WA Industrial Relations Act 1979`
        IF `if it substitutes another day for Easter Sunday solely because Easter Sunday falls on a weekend`
            THEN `this Act: a substitute day for Easter Sunday because it falls on a weekend has no effect (s 3(3))`
        IF NOT `if it is inconsistent with the provision of or under the Act`
            THEN `no inconsistency: both apply`
        IF `if that provision is in a proclamation under s 7 or 8`
            THEN `the proclamation (s 9)`
        OTHERWISE `my industrial instrument (s 3(1))`

-- s 3(2): "A provision of an industrial instrument relating to public holidays applies to Easter Sunday regardless of
-- whether the instrument makes reference to Easter Sunday."
@export Does my WA award's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday (s 3(2))?
GIVEN `if my instrument is made under the WA Industrial Relations Act 1979` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your award or agreement was made under the Industrial Relations Act 1979 (WA)
      `if it has a provision relating to public holidays` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the instrument has any provision about public holidays (penalty rates, days off, and so on)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my award's public holiday provision apply to Easter Sunday` IF
    `if my instrument is made under the WA Industrial Relations Act 1979` AND `if it has a provision relating to public holidays`
